{
  "info": {
    "name": "PayWarden — zero-trust payment firewall",
    "description": "End-to-end, self-checking tour of the PayWarden API: STEP-UP and dual-control approvals with single-use TOTP, attacks being denied, security controls, the MCP agent channel and the audit chain.\n\nRun the whole collection against a server in demo mode (`PAYWARDEN_DEMO_MODE=true`) with the `PayWarden — local` environment. Folders 1 and 2 each wait up to 30 s for a fresh TOTP window, because codes are single-use (a full run takes under a minute). Amounts and payees are randomised per run; repeated runs on the same database within 24 h can eventually hit the agent's rolling daily limit (LIM-04), which is the control working as designed.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Health & mandate",
      "description": "Service mode and the agent's spend mandate. Also seeds random run values so the collection can be re-run without tripping the duplicate-payment control.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const r = Math.floor(Math.random() * 900000) + 100000;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"run\", r);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"amtSmall\", `${100 + r % 800}.${String(r % 100).padStart(2, \"0\")}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"amtAgent\", `${100 + (r >> 3) % 800}.${String((r >> 2) % 100).padStart(2, \"0\")}`);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"amtHigh\", `${5001 + r % 999}.00`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const h = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"reports PayPal and AI mode\", () => pm.expect(h).to.have.keys(\"ok\", \"paypal_mode\", \"ai_engine\", \"demo_mode\", \"redaction\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"security headers present\", () => {",
                  "  [\"Strict-Transport-Security\", \"Content-Security-Policy\", \"X-Frame-Options\", \"X-Content-Type-Options\"]",
                  "    .forEach((k) => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has(k), k).to.be.true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Agent mandate",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/policy",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "policy"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{makerToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"auto-execute limit is 1000.00\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().per_txn_auto_limit).to.eql(\"1000.00\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 · STEP-UP payout (new payee)",
      "description": "First payment to a new payee needs one human with TOTP.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Analyse invoice → STEP_UP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/agent/analyse",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "agent",
                "analyse"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{makerToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"document\": \"INVOICE PM-{{run}}\\nFrom: Postman Designs {{run}}\\nEmail: designs.{{run}}@example.com\\nCountry: US\\nTotal due: ${{amtSmall}} USD\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const p = pm.response.json().proposals[0];",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"p1Id\", p.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"p1Binding\", p.binding);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"verdict is STEP_UP\", () => pm.expect(p.verdict).to.eql(\"STEP_UP\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"status is PENDING\", () => pm.expect(p.status).to.eql(\"PENDING\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"payee is masked\", () => pm.expect(p.payee_masked).to.include(\"*\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"binding is a 64-hex HMAC\", () => pm.expect(p.binding).to.match(/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
